---@class aws.route53resolver.UpdateResolverEndpointRequest
---@field ResolverEndpointId aws.route53resolver.ResourceId The ID of the Resolver endpoint that you want to update.
---@field Name? aws.route53resolver.Name The name of the Resolver endpoint that you want to update.
---@field ResolverEndpointType? aws.route53resolver.ResolverEndpointType|string Specifies the endpoint type for what type of IP address the endpoint uses to forward DNS queries.
---@field UpdateIpAddresses? aws.route53resolver.UpdateIpAddresses Specifies the IPv6 address when you update the Resolver endpoint from IPv4 to dual-stack. If you don't specify an IPv6 address, one will be automatically chosen from your subnet.
---@field Protocols? aws.route53resolver.ProtocolList The protocols you want to use for the endpoint. DoH-FIPS is applicable for default inbound endpoints only.
---@field RniEnhancedMetricsEnabled? aws.route53resolver.RniEnhancedMetricsEnabled Updates whether RNI enhanced metrics are enabled for the Resolver endpoints. When set to true, one-minute granular metrics are published in CloudWatch for each RNI associated with this endpoint. When set to false, metrics are not published.
---@field TargetNameServerMetricsEnabled? aws.route53resolver.TargetNameServerMetricsEnabled Updates whether target name server metrics are enabled for the outbound Resolver endpoints. When set to true, one-minute granular metrics are published in CloudWatch for each target name server associated with this endpoint. When set to false, metrics are not published. This setting is not supported for inbound Resolver endpoints.
---@field Dns64Enabled? aws.route53resolver.Dns64Enabled Specifies whether DNS64 is enabled for the inbound Resolver endpoint. When set to true, Route 53 Resolver synthesizes AAAA (IPv6) records for IPv4-only services by prepending the 64:ff9b::/96 prefix to the IPv4 address. This enables IPv6-only clients that send queries through the inbound endpoint to reach IPv4-only services. DNS64 works with NAT64 to provide complete IPv6-to-IPv4 translation.
---@field Ipv6InternetAccessEnabled? aws.route53resolver.Ipv6InternetAccessEnabled Specifies whether IPv6 internet access is enabled for the outbound Resolver endpoint. When set to true, the endpoint elastic network interfaces (ENIs) can forward DNS queries to public IPv6 targets through an internet gateway.

